    "content": "Under the International Astronomical Union (IAU) definition, there are **eight planets** in our solar system.\n\nThe eight planets, in order from the Sun, are:\n\n1. Mercury  \n2. Venus  \n3. Earth  \n4. Mars  \n5. Jupiter  \n6. Saturn  \n7. Uranus  \n8. Neptune  \n\nThis classification was established in 2006 when Pluto was reclassified as a \"dwarf planet\" because it does not meet all three criteria for a planet set by the IAU, particularly the requirement to have \"cleared the neighborhood\" around its orbit.",
